  "rationale": "R6 exposed a systematic exactly-once defect under ISS out-of-order defender resignation messages. When a defender RE arrived before the echo of SkatAI's already-sent card, reconciliation correctly left the first effect pending, but the client re-ran inference because RE changed the reconstructed request position. The journal allowed a second nonterminal effect for the same game because its position hash differed. This produced duplicate HT and HK sends in two R6 games; ISS later rejected the duplicates with _you_do_not_have_card errors. Those table_error events were parsed but not treated as gate failures, so both games could still reach SCORED. V2 now enforces at most one nonterminal material effect per game, skips inference while one is pending, and fails closed on active-game table_error with mirrored PROTOCOL_FAILURE evidence.",
